 ## Diagnosis record
 
@@ -97,4 +98,12 @@
 - Mining completed with 18 copper drops, then repeatedly exited with no gain because inventory remained full. The action wrapper discarded the skill's result and exposed only incidental navigation/discard logs. Native source `5a12c26` now reports measured drops, partial/no progress and storage blockers; nine regressions pass.
 - The installed Mineflayer metadata handler assigns every entity's air to `bot.oxygenLevel`. Actual dependency replay proves foreign zero-air metadata can overwrite own full air. Native source `6904c3a` derives modern oxygen from the own entity before synchronous safety consumers read it; real low-air rescue remains active. The unchanged-state scheduler wakes at 10/40 seconds in replay, but false oxygen churn resets it every 10 seconds; the fix addresses that source without suppressing real oxygen changes.
 - Native inventory now reports available storage slots (unknown stays unknown), and plugin source `b5bbb8f` retains this fact in bounded recovery context. The complete plugin suite now passes 100 tests.
-- Further observed: Mineflayer can drop a crafting output when inventory is full while reporting completion, and the recipe planner can falsely request oak when spruce is carried. These require separately tested native fixes before the final deployment/observation pass.
+- Native source `ce78380` now reserves crafting storage before consuming ingredients and confirms modern output against the existing authoritative full-inventory synchronization; legacy transaction acknowledgements remain supported. Source `60c2d1e` shares generic wood eligibility with actual recipes, allocates real stocked wood/planks and preserves species-specific recipes. Native suite: 293 passed; contribution suite: 299 passed. These were deployed together as live body `bb30541`.
+- Post-deployment idle observation confirmed stable decision revision and 60-to-120-second retry backoff, instead of false oxygen-driven 10-second resets. The body had no new task in that window: health alone is not proof of autonomy.
+- The main model then repeatedly observed and narrated an unsupported slab-to-plank conversion without dispatching. There was no tool-cap or endpoint refusal. Plugin task metadata mixed autonomous permission with broad prohibitions on recovery from feedback, and observation results did not restate execution eligibility. Source `ca4759e` separates direct user relay from persistent autonomous recovery and reduces the description from 1,123 to 437 tokens; it prohibits interruptions for stationary crafting/model latency. Source `c92a327` adds plugin-owned, conditional next-action guidance after observations. Disabled/stopped/busy/stale/disconnected/unknown states cannot suggest a new automatic action; latest human stop/pause still wins. The full plugin suite passes 118 tests. Both changes were reloaded through the existing plugin lifecycle, with the live tool registry confirming the new contract.
+- Subsequent passive observation confirmed the main model dispatched its own wood/tool task. The executor rejected the unsupported slab conversion, collected real wood and received server-confirmed crafting output: 12 spruce planks, 16 sticks, one wooden pickaxe, then one crafting table. These are output events, not a claim that all supplies remain carried simultaneously. The next autonomous task left the village area and mined 10 coal, reported by the measured mining wrapper. Health and food remained 20/20 in the sampled state. No diagnostic tasks, chat or spells were injected.
+- Live collection exposed two additional executor problems. Required-argument command names in reasoning were parsed as calls, and a goal-stop hook ran before argument validation. Tree-canopy ENTOMBED transitions also interrupted real `getWood` progress. These are native fixes, separate from the earlier material gains: source `992f50b` gives actual current-generation tree harvesting a bounded eight-second canopy grace, retaining an observed dig target for at most three seconds. Vital danger, SEALED, wet/stone/unknown geometry and persistent traps still allow rescue.
+- The local LLM service remained the resident Strata/Qwen process at `127.0.0.1:18030`. Two different no-tool diagnostic requests returned their exact distinct markers in 1.22 and 0.91 seconds. Runtime metrics show fresh prompt processing for repeated narrative turns; no generic response memoization was found. Short probes do not establish long-context decision quality.
+- Source `ff97159` selects actual invocations instead of command-name references and moves goal interruption after validation. Lifecycle commands use their own lines; six tracked profiles and the actual default/base/trial inheritance examples were aligned with that rule. Further live replay exposed repeated standalone JSON-shaped calls (`!mineOres({"ore":"coal"})`). Source `73b4a56` keeps them non-executable but records metadata-derived positional syntax and a validated correction in internal history, so the model can correct its next call without stopping the goal or publishing debug text.
+- Read-only logs also confirmed a circular wait: soft MAROONED blocked task navigation while an external task froze the corresponding march. Source `e4a5816` shares the ownership decision between `goToGoal`, `goToPosition`, ore tunneling and `mineOres`; a frozen march cannot reserve task navigation, while a real mobility owner, standalone recovery and vital danger retain their existing gates. Routes, line-of-sight, digging safety and protection checks remain intact. Source `f0380ce` prevents a fresh external task's mine descent from silently returning to an old bed anchor; standalone/expired leases preserve the legacy entrance behavior.
+- Final native regression: 368 passed; contribution regression: 374 passed; legacy mineDown contract test: 1 passed. Plugin regression remains 118 passed, and host callback/media regression 195 passed. Native live revision `3a941db` includes these fixes; the established lifecycle reloaded only the Minecraft body and plugin, retaining the local model, main process and runtime arbitration data. Post-reload progress and remaining limitations are recorded in the companion contribution diagnosis.
